Article 10
Every person who hears, sees, or knows of the occurrence of violence against women and children is obligated to make efforts in accordance with their capacity to:
a. Prevent and stop the ongoing act of violence;
b. Provide protection to the victim;
c. Provide emergency assistance; and/or
d. Assist in the process of submitting an application for the determination of protection Kk

Article 8
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 7 letter a, include:
a. establishing, implementing policies, programs, and conducting cooperation activities in the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
b. facilitating the establishment of institutional protection of women and children from acts of violence and providing support for facilities and infrastructure;
c. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with regional financial capacity;
d. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. providing protection services for women and children victims of acts of violence;
f. encouraging and increasing community participation; and
g. appointing parents and/or substitute family caregivers as a protection measure for children who are victims of acts of violence.
(2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent shall establish programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in one Regional Action Plan as a basis for Regional Apparatus in implementing the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.
(4) Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 21
(1) The Regional Government develops cooperation patterns in order to achieve the objectives of protecting women and children from acts of violence in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) is conducted between the Regional Government and:
a. Central Government;
b. Provincial Government;
c. Other Regency/City Governments;
d. Higher Education Institutions;
e. Social and religious institutions;
f. Non-Governmental Organizations; and/or
g. Media.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) includes:
a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. return and social reintegration; and
d. provision of evidence and witnesses.
(4) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) is implemented in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

CHAPTER IX
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 23
(1) The Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(2) Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. guidelines and standards of fulfillment;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. coordination;
d. monitoring;
e. evaluation; and
f. reporting.

Article 3
The purpose of protecting women and children from acts of violence is to:
a. Prevent acts of violence against women and children, including trafficking in persons;
b. Eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. Protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. Provide services to women and children who are victims of acts of violence, reporters, and witnesses; and
e. Strengthen women and children who are victims of acts of violence so that they are more empowered, both physically, psychologically, socially, and economically.

Article 16
(1) Prevention of the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children as referred to in Article 15, shall be implemented by Regional Apparatus whose duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. education;
d. manpower;
e. population and civil registration;
f. law;
g. women's empowerment and child protection;
h. cooperatives and Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises;
i. mental and spiritual; and
j. public peace and order.
(2) Prevention of acts of violence by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in an integrated and sustainable manner based on the Regional Long-Term Development Plan and Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.

Article 20
Community Participation is carried out by means of:
a. Fostering community awareness of cases of violence against women and children;
b. Encouraging the community to actively participate in providing information and reporting acts of violence against women and children;
c. Fostering local wisdom in handling cases of violence;
d. Organizing strengthening of community groups in handling acts of violence against women and children;
e. Disseminating information about laws and regulations related to acts of violence against women and children.

Article 15
(1) The Regional Government shall carry out empowerment and awareness-raising for families, parents, and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.
(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness as referred to in paragraph (1), it shall be implemented by means of:
a. providing material on the prevention of acts of violence against women and children in both formal and informal education;
b. opening/providing access to obtain education, training, funding, income enhancement and social services in accordance with applicable provisions;
c. opening employment opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and concern towards the prevention and protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, educational institutions, and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children; and
g. opening an integrated service system for the protection of women and children from acts of violence in every urban village (kelurahan).

CHAPTER IV
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 5
Women and children victims of acts of violence shall receive the following rights:
a. The right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
b. The right to recovery;
c. The right to determine their own decisions;
d. The right to obtain information;
e. The right to confidentiality;
f. The right to social rehabilitation;
g. The right to complaint handling that is prompt, appropriate, comfortable and in accordance with needs;
h. The right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. The right to assistance; and
j. The right to a sense of security.

NERA TUNGGAL
REGENT OF POHUWATO
GORONTALO PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF POHUWATO REGENCY NUMBER 6 OF 2018
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY
THE REGENT OF POHUWATO,

Considering : a. that in order to restore the dignity and honor of women and children victims of violence and to restore their social function, it is necessary to undertake efforts for protection, empowerment of women, and rehabilitation of children victims of violence;
b. that based on Article 12 of Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, empowerment of women and protection of children constitute mandatory governmental affairs for regional governments;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence.

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 38 of 2000 concerning the Establishment of Gorontalo Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2000 Number 258, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4060);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606) as amended by Law of the Republic of Indonesia Number 17 of 2016 on the Stipulation of Government Regulation in Lieu of Law Number 1 of 2016 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection into Law (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2016 Number 237, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5946);
4. Law Number 6 of 2003 concerning the Establishment of Bone Bolango Regency and Pohuwato Regency in Gorontalo Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2003 Number 26, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4269);
5. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
6. Law of the Republic of Indonesia Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);
7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning the Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
8. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Violence in the Household (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);

With mutual agreement,

Article 2
The protection of women and children from acts of violence is organized based on the principles of
a. Humanity;
b. Justice and gender equality;
c. Non-discrimination;
d. Order and legal certainty;
e. Transparency;
f. Protection.

